1:["$","main",null,{"className":"site article-page","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"article-frame","children":[["$","$La",null,{"className":"desktop-brand","href":"/","children":"Thinkinghaus"}],["$","article",null,{"className":"article-column","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"article-header","children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"The Usefulness of an Empty Mind"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"August 6, 2026"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"3 minutes"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article-body","children":[[["$","p","0-One of my favorite books—favorite manuals, really—is Zen Mind, Beginner's Mind, a book by the Zen monk Shunryu Suzuki.",{"children":"One of my favorite books—favorite manuals, really—is Zen Mind, Beginner's Mind, a book by the Zen monk Shunryu Suzuki."}],["$","p","1-He says, “In the beginner’s mind there are many possibilities, in the expert’s, there are few.”",{"children":"He says, “In the beginner’s mind there are many possibilities, in the expert’s, there are few.”"}],["$","p","2-Well, expertise is darn useful: it recognizes patterns, avoids old mistakes, it knows which details matter. But it can also become a kind of compression. The more I know about something, the less of it I may actually see. I see the category before I see the thing.",{"children":"Well, expertise is darn useful: it recognizes patterns, avoids old mistakes, it knows which details matter. But it can also become a kind of compression. The more I know about something, the less of it I may actually see. I see the category before I see the thing."}],["$","p","3-Suzuki isn't telling us to strive for stupidity. Beginner’s mind isn't the absence of experience or knowledge. It's a way of standing in both without letting the shoes turn to cement. Easier said than done for sure.",{"children":"Suzuki isn't telling us to strive for stupidity. Beginner’s mind isn't the absence of experience or knowledge. It's a way of standing in both without letting the shoes turn to cement. Easier said than done for sure."}],["$","p","4-The book is assembled from talks and feels spoken. As you move through it, ideas appear, disappear, return slightly changed…sometimes an explanation leaves me less certain than when it began. Seems appropriate.",{"children":"The book is assembled from talks and feels spoken. As you move through it, ideas appear, disappear, return slightly changed…sometimes an explanation leaves me less certain than when it began. Seems appropriate."}],["$","p","5-He talks about posture, breathing, repetition, effort, and the ordinary difficulty of sitting still. The spiritual life he describes is visceral. It’s in my hands, my spine, my willingness to sit and practice without turning it into an achievement.",{"children":"He talks about posture, breathing, repetition, effort, and the ordinary difficulty of sitting still. The spiritual life he describes is visceral. It’s in my hands, my spine, my willingness to sit and practice without turning it into an achievement."}],["$","p","6-But I like practices that produce results! I want to know whether I am progressing! Even when I’m actively trying to become less ambitious, I can become ambitious about becoming less ambitious.",{"children":"But I like practices that produce results! I want to know whether I am progressing! Even when I’m actively trying to become less ambitious, I can become ambitious about becoming less ambitious."}],["$","p","7-His advice is to return to the activity itself. Why sit? Because you are sitting. Breathe because you are breathing. Do the thing without constantly stepping outside it to decide what it means, what it means about you. I cannot say I consistently live this way, but I deeply respect and value the freedom in it.",{"children":"His advice is to return to the activity itself. Why sit? Because you are sitting. Breathe because you are breathing. Do the thing without constantly stepping outside it to decide what it means, what it means about you. I cannot say I consistently live this way, but I deeply respect and value the freedom in it."}],"$Lb","$Lc","$Ld","$Le"],null]}],"$Lf"]}]]}]}]
b:["$","p","8-Beginner’s mind may be less about innocence than repeatedly setting down what I think I know. Not throwing it away, just…loosening my grip long enough for something else to appear.",{"children":"Beginner’s mind may be less about innocence than repeatedly setting down what I think I know. Not throwing it away, just…loosening my grip long enough for something else to appear."}]
c:["$","p","9-This book is not a manual for mastering Zen. It's a manual for taking aim at that part of me that wants to master it. Which makes it a manual for mastering Zen. Which makes it…",{"children":"This book is not a manual for mastering Zen. It's a manual for taking aim at that part of me that wants to master it. Which makes it a manual for mastering Zen. Which makes it…"}]
d:["$","p","10-This book does not make Zen easy.",{"children":"This book does not make Zen easy."}]
e:["$","p","11-It does makes simplicity seem like enough for me to work on.",{"children":"It does makes simplicity seem like enough for me to work on."}]
